    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The equation separates two carrier steps: encoding makes the dense feature field, then window partitioning keeps the field as tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into the dense feature field named F. The first equality names the dense carrier before any thought update happens. Window partitioning then turns that same field into X without dropping tokens. The camera closes on the partition because that is where the dense carrier becomes window tokens.",
      "evidence": [
